Suggestion 1. Optimize using a single pass with prefix sums The nested loops should be replaced by a single pass using a more efficient counting method. Calculate the prefix sums of 'w' and 'b' beforehand and then use a sliding window over those sums to find the required segments.
```java
public static void main(String[] args){
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
    int w = sc.nextInt();
    int b = sc.nextInt();
    String wb = "wbwbwwbwbwbw", s = "";
    for(int i = 0; i < 20; i++) s += wb;
    int sl = s.length();

    int[] wPrefix = new int[sl + 1];
    int[] bPrefix = new int[sl + 1];

    for(int i = 0; i < sl; i++) {
        wPrefix[i + 1] = wPrefix[i] + (s.charAt(i) == 'w' ? 1 : 0);
        bPrefix[i + 1] = bPrefix[i] + (s.charAt(i) == 'b' ? 1 : 0);
    }

    for(int i = 0; i <= sl; i++) {
        for(int j = i + 1; j <= sl; j++) {
            int wnum = wPrefix[j] - wPrefix[i];
            int bnum = bPrefix[j] - bPrefix[i];
            if(wnum == w && bnum == b) {
                System.out.println("Yes");
                return;
            }
        }
    }
    System.out.println("No");
}
```

